d","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:08d566a4f9e7a1dc448257cbcdda3afa296e74ec31ac50cf0e394429ee2ab43c","file":"preprints/Midpoint-convexity-from-two-recursive-potentials-September-27-2026/build/sections/variable.tex","line":56,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"5fffbccbe47c9b520cfc4e779c035da46bd08f4cb26e4af9daa03a112fa5c6e2","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Midpoint-convexity-from-two-recursive-potentials-September-27-2026/build/sections/variable.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:08d566a4f9e7a1dc448257cbcdda3afa296e74ec31ac50cf0e394429ee2ab43c","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Midpoint-convexity-from-two-recursive-potentials-September-27-2026/build/sections/variable.tex#L56"},"statement_kind":"proposition","text":"\\label{var:space}\nThe recursion \\eqref{var:recursion} defines a norm equivalent to the\nusual $\\ell_{p_h}(T_h)$ norm.  In particular, $E_h$ is complete and\nreflexive, with separable dual.  The space $X_{\\mathrm v}$ is complete\nand reflexive, its dual is separable, and vectors with finite total\ncoordinate support are dense in it.  Every finite coordinate\nprojection is bounded and has finite rank."}
